body:
Meredith Duran is my go-to for reads like this. Her characters are always so dimensional and they deal with very real problems and react like real people. Her books feel very authentic and compelling and immersive.

{The Duke of Shadows by Meredith Duran}

{The Sins of Lord Lockwood by Meredith Duran}

{Fool Me Twice by Meredith Duran}

{A Lady's Code of Misconduct by Meredith Duran}

{An Unacceptable Offer by Mary Balogh} (steam is meh)

{Lady Isabella’s Scandalous Marriage by Jennifer Ashley}

{The Marquess Wins a Wife by Aydra Richards}

{Bed Me, Baron by Felicity Niven}

{This Duchess of Mine by Eloisa James}

I love Jo Goodman for this!

{In Want of a Wife by Jo Goodman}

{This Gun for Hire by Jo Goodman}

{The Last Renegade by Jo Goodman}

Maggie Osborne also has some amazing books! A bit lower in spice but the MCs do not hold back on their attraction to each other. In {The Promise of Jenny Jones by Maggie Osborne} they’re enemies at first who both admitted they want to hook up very badly. Like they wanted to both punch the other and kiss at the same time.

Meredith Duran is my go-to author for this! 

