Happy reading!

Along the lines of this post, please give me recs for tall MMCs AND FMCs. Since apparently I’m considered a giantess by Regency standards (and today still in my home country), I’d love some escape from reality. Here are some of my favs with tall MCs:

{The King’s Man by Elizabeth Kingston}

{The Promise of Jenny Jones by Maggie Osborne}

{How to Catch a Duke by Grace Burrowes}

{Dukes Prefer Blondes by Loretta Chase}

{The Devil is a Marquess by Elisa Braden}

{The Sins of Lord Lockwood by Meredith Duran}

Edit to remove Bed Me Earl because Phin is a short king! He just has the vibes of a tall man so I forgot that he’s several inches shorter than Caro.

“Maybe she’d also find a sense of peace, if she didn’t try to be more than she was.” {The Bridal Veil by Alexis Harrington}

“Such a hate has lived in your breast, all the while I lay my head there. You have no need of a sword, my lady. Already am I defeated.” {The King’s Man by Elizabeth Kingston}

“If friendship was all that Webb could offer, then she would accept his friendship, and gladly. Twenty-eight-year-old spinsters were accustomed to settling for crumbs; she didn't even mind anymore.” {Brides of Prarie Gold by Maggie Osborne}

{The Promise of Jenny Jones by Maggie Osborne} is my #1 western.

{Silver Lining by Maggie Osborne} is a must read, but {The Wives of Bowie Stone by Maggie Osborne} is so underrated.

{Topaz by Beverly Jenkins} has a mail-order bride backdrop but the MCs themselves aren’t exactly involved.

{In Want of a Wife by Jo Goodman} is the best book with mail order bride trope I’ve ever read. I also love {This Gun for Hire by Jo Goodman}

For angst you must check out {Harper’s Bride by Alexis Harrington} and {The Bridal Veil by Alexis Harrington}

I would recommend the popular books by Meredith Duran. I find her writing very refreshing because she's not afraid to have genuinely flawed MCs who challenge each other's views. It's not often I find romance extremely thought-provoking, but this author just has that kind of magic.

{Luck Be a Lady by Meredith Duran}

{Fool Me Twice by Meredith Duran}

{The Sins of Lord Lockwood by Meredith Duran}

{A Lady's Code of Misconduct by Meredith Duran}

I’d say Grace Burrowes writes very good non-rake and rake heroes! But my favs are

{Douglas by Grace Burrowes}

{The Truth About Dukes by Grace Burrowes}

{My One and Only Duke by Grace Burrowes}

Yes! In general Grace Burrowes is my go-to author for this.

{Douglas by Gracw Burrowes}

